{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Have we yet, etc.</b> They doubled the expression <b>a portion and an inheritance</b>, to allude to two things: the first is the portion pertaining to them in the inheritance of their mother, who had already died, and the second is the inheritance of their father. And they concluded that they have no expectation from either of them, and the proof — ״הֲלֹא נָכְרִיּוֹת נֶחְשַׁבְנוּ לוֹ״ — he has already sold us; this is your sign that we are not in his estimation at the level of children, and consequently he will decree that they not inherit from him. Even though according to the laws of the nations it is possible for daughters to inherit, and On proves it, and as in the case of Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel and his sister (Shabbat 116a)." "And their saying <b>and he has utterly consumed</b> (וַיֹּאכַל גַּם אָכוֹל) — two consumptions: one is the inheritance of their mother's ketubah, and the second is what Jacob labored fourteen years on their behalf."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:13.838863299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}